WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.862
October 24th, 1946.

00:00:01.872 --> 00:00:04.171
White Sands, New Mexico.

00:00:04.181 --> 00:00:06.032
A rocket is ready.

00:00:06.132 --> 00:00:07.842
It's a captured V-2.

00:00:07.879 --> 00:00:09.069
In its nose:

00:00:09.079 --> 00:00:11.508
a 35 millimeter movie camera.

00:00:11.518 --> 00:00:13.411
It takes one frame every second and

00:00:13.421 --> 00:00:14.218
a half.

00:00:14.228 --> 00:00:17.181
The rocket climbs 65 miles, about 105

00:00:17.191 --> 00:00:20.995
kilometers, past the
line where space begins.

00:00:21.108 --> 00:00:23.048
Then it smashes into the desert.

00:00:23.058 --> 00:00:25.109
But the film cassette survives.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:26.097
On the film:

00:00:26.107 --> 00:00:28.084
grainy pictures of Earth, from above the

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.074
atmosphere.

00:00:29.084 --> 00:00:31.272
Our first look at Earth from space.
